# Cloudflare local state. `.dev.vars` holds real secrets (e.g. USAGE_HASH_KEY) for
# `wrangler dev`; it must never be committed. `.wrangler/` is local build/state cache.
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*
!.dev.vars.example
.wrangler/

# The Canonical Adoption Index's ENTIRE persistence (new15 R-1; ADR 0061 INV-R7):
# the SQLite database, its -wal/-shm sidecars, the content-addressed blob store, work
# and dead-letter dirs, and run reports. This lands in the SAME commit as the store that
# writes it, not later: the first real compile run offers `adoption-index.sqlite-wal` to
# `git status`, and a WAL file is exactly the kind of thing a hurried `git add -A`
# commits. A boundary no gate reads is not a boundary, so R-1 also asserts
# `git status --porcelain` is empty after a real run.
.var/

# A local scratch clone of a FORK of cline/marketplace, used once to open upstream PR #49
# (`marketplace/` → saintl1022/marketplace, upstream cline/marketplace). Commit ec9d27c
# (PR #314) committed it as a bare `160000` gitlink with no `.gitmodules` entry — an
# unregistered submodule, which is the one submodule state git cannot restore: a fresh
# clone gets an empty directory and `git submodule update` has nothing to read. It is
# referenced by no script, build, gate or workflow, so registering it as a real submodule
# would force every CallLint clone to fetch a fork of someone else's marketplace to build
# nothing. Untracked instead; the submission it produced lives in the upstream PR, and the
# SSOT records that as `cline` / `PENDING_UPSTREAM`.
/marketplace/

# The distribution watcher's snapshot. Produced by running scripts/check-official-sources.mjs
# locally, and NEVER a repo file: usage-report.yml restores the previous snapshot from an
# Actions artifact, and check-public-copy forbids a `git commit` in that workflow. Left
# untracked-but-unignored it was one `git add -A` away from being committed, at which point
# the baseline would come from the working tree instead of the artifact and every run would
# diff against a stale, hand-editable snapshot.
/artifacts/distribution-watch/
